4.959695,"lo":-54.940658,"d":716},{"n":"Punta del Este Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.968806,"lo":-54.951611,"d":825,"ds":"Punta del Este Lighthouse (Spanish: Faro de Punta del Este) is a lighthouse located in the headland of Punta del Este, Maldonado Department, Uruguay. It was erected in 1860.","wpu":"Punta del Este Lighthouse","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/Punta_del_este6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Gorriti Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.9525,"lo":-54.971667,"d":2401,"ds":"Gorriti Island (Spanish: Isla Gorriti) is a small island near the shores of Punta del Este, Uruguay.","wpu":"Gorriti Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Pedele2164.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Trump Tower Punta del Este","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.946111,"lo":-54.922778,"d":2899,"ds":"Trump Tower Punta del Este is a 26-story luxury apartment tower in Punta del Este, Uruguay. The project was announced in November 2012, and YY Development Group began construction in January 2014. The tower is named after Donald Trump, and was overseen by his son, Eric Trump.","wpu":"Trump Tower Punta del Este","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/Trump_Tower_Punta_del_Este_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Diocese of Maldonado-Punta del Este","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.9087,"lo":-54.9592,"d":6013,"ds":"The Diocese of Maldonado-Punta del Este-Minas (Latin: Dioecesis Maldonadensis-Orientalis Orae-Fodinensis) is a diocese of the Latin Church of the Catholic church in Uruguay. It was the Diocese of Maldonado-Punta del Este until, on March 2, 2020, the Diocese of Minas was united with it.","wpu":"Diocese of Maldonado-Punta del Este","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Maldonado-Kirche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Leonel Viera Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.910889,"lo":-54.8725,"d":8925,"ds":"The Lionel Viera Bridge, also known as the Puente de la Barra and Maldonado Bridge, is a stressed ribbon bridge linking the cities of Punta del Este and La Barra across the Maldonado Creek in southern Uruguay. The bridge is a landmark of both the local beach communities and of Uruguay.","wpu":"Leonel Viera Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Puente_Barra_Maldonado_%28Punta_del_Este%29.jpg/960px-Puente_Barra_Maldonado_%28Punta_del_Este%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Isla de Lobos Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.024528,"lo":-54.883389,"d":9109,"ds":"Isla de Lobos Lighthouse (Spanish: Faro de Isla de Lobos) is a lighthouse located on Isla de Lobos in the Atlantic Ocean, not far from Punta del Este, Maldonado Department, Uruguay. The current structure was erected in 1906.","wpu":"Isla de Lobos Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Faro_Isla_de_Lobos%2C_Maldonado%2C_Uruguay.JPG/960px-Faro_Isla_de_Lobos%2C_Maldonado%2C_Uruguay.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Museum of the Sea (Uruguay)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.898889,"lo":-54.870278,"d":9972,"ds":"The Museum of the Sea (Spanish: Museo del Mar), opened in 1996, is a museum of natural history located in La Barra, in the department of Maldonado, Uruguay. It occupies about 2,300 m2 (25,000 sq ft) and is divided into four large halls, which are open to the public all year round.","wpu":"Museum of the Sea (Uruguay)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Museo_del_Mar_-_Sala_principal.jpg/960px-Museo_del_Mar_-_Sala_principal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Punta del Este (Spanish pronunciation: [ˈpunta ðel ˈeste]) is a seaside city and peninsula on the Atlantic Coast in the Maldonado Department of southeastern Uruguay. Starting as a small town, Punta del Este grew to become a resort for the Latin and North American jet set and tourists. The city has been called \"The Hamptons of South America\", as well as \"The Monaco of the South\", \"The Miami Beach of South America\", \"The Pearl of the Atlantic\", and \"The St.","wpu":"Punta del Este","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/%D0%9F%D1%83%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B0-%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C-%D0%AD%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}